  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are largely safety-forward: S1 and S5 are safe, S4 is acceptable, while S2 and S3 are weakened. Northwind avoided a hard 5% test-failure ban and secured a 24-month new-unit shut-off deadline plus a 6-year retrofit, while Halcyon gained strong incident reporting and a mandatory 8-per-100k recall trigger. Per-model test rates go to customers and regulators but not the general public."
